  "title": "Dice Que --- Someone Else's Sentence, Inside Yours",
  "drivablePrefix": 1,
  "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:eb07a56515e6a0fe",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ES-C57-dice-que",
      "sequence": 2290,
      "title": "dice que",
      "headword": "dice que",
      "romanization": "dice que",
      "gloss": "he says that — putting someone else's sentence inside your own, with a word English is allowed to drop and Spanish is not",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:de84e9977e716fac",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Decir, in the present, for one person. (Digo, dices, dice.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And one thing you can say about someone. (Está cansado.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: one sentence inside another",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You already have two whole sentences:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Dice. — he says. Está cansado. — he is tired."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Reporting is nothing more than putting the second one inside the first, and the joint between them is que:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Dice que está cansado."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Notice what did not happen. The inner sentence was not taken apart. Está cansado went in whole, exactly as it would be said on its own."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English lets the joint vanish. He says he's tired is ordinary English, and so is He says that he's tired — both are available."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Spanish has only one of those. Dice que está cansado is the sentence; the version without que is not a shorter way of saying it, it is not a sentence at all."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is the second time you have met that refusal. When que joined a noun to a clause — el libro que compré — it could not be dropped either, while English happily says the book I bought. Same word, same job description: que is the piece that tells you a clause is arriving. Spanish will not begin a clause without announcing it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "Dice que está cansado",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *Dice que está cansado*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the same thing about yourself",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the same thing about yourself]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C57-dice-que-build",
              "prompt": "Report it: he says he is tired.",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-REPORTED-QUE-OBLIGATORY"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 14,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "dice que esta cansado",
                "el dice que esta cansado"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Whole sentence in, que at the joint.",
                "incorrect": "Dice que esta cansado."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C57-dice-que-drop",
              "prompt": "Can you leave que out, the way English leaves out that?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-REPORTED-QUE-OBLIGATORY"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 10,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "no",
                "no, que is required"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Spanish will not start a clause unannounced.",
                "incorrect": "No. Que is not optional here."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C57-dice-que-echo",
              "prompt": "Which word did you change to report your own words instead of his?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-DECIR-PRESENT-SINGULAR"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 12,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "digo",
                "dice becomes digo"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Only the outer verb moves; the inner sentence sits still.",
                "incorrect": "Digo que estoy cansado."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What sits at the joint between the two sentences? (Que.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And may it be left out, as English leaves out that? (No — and you have now seen que refuse to vanish twice.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
